# DocsLayout Molde Shadow (冻结)

**Do not change** the docs shell shadow architecture unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Shadow placement (fixed)

Molde left shadow (`effect-molde-level` → `--effect-shadow-molde`) is **always** on the content shell, never toggled by nav state:

| Page | Element | Classes |
|------|---------|---------|
| Doc pages | `contentShell` | `contentShell` + `contentShellDoc` + `effect-molde-level` |
| Explore | `contentShell` | `contentShell` + `effect-molde-level` |

`main` is a **transparent container only** — no `effect-molde-level`, no `box-shadow`, no `background`.

## CSS constraints (fixed)

```css
/* main — must stay overflow: visible or left shadow is clipped */
.main { overflow: visible; background: transparent; }

/* contentShell — carries background + molde shadow */
.contentShell { background: var(--content-background); }
```

- Do **not** move shadow back to `main` when section nav is collapsed.
- Do **not** conditionally add/remove `effect-molde-level` based on `sectionNavOpen`.
- Do **not** set `main { overflow: hidden }` — it clips `contentShell` box-shadow.

## Section nav shadow (separate)

`.layoutSectionNavOpen .sectionNavShell` keeps its own right-edge shadow — independent from content molde shadow. Do not merge or duplicate onto `contentShell`.
